<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Betico Croes</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1938">1938</a>–<a href="/years/1986">1986</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a> · Also known as Gilberto François Croes</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Betico Croes, born Gilberto François Croes, was an Aruban politician who led the movement for Aruba's separation from the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-the-netherlands">Netherlands</a> Antilles. He founded the People's Electoral Movement in 1971 and won a referendum for separation in 1977, securing status aparte for Aruba within the Kingdom of the Netherlands from 1 January 1986. Badly injured in a car crash the night before, he died in November 1986.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/betico-croes.jpg" alt="Betico Croes" width="320" height="572" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Rob Bogaerts for Anefo · CC BY-SA 3.0 nl · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Betico_Croes_1982cr.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
